  "id": "point-of-subjective-equality",
  "term": "point of subjective equality",
  "definition": "The point of subjective equality is the comparison value at which a person judges two stimuli as equal, even if they may differ objectively. In this study, it was estimated from each person’s psychometric function in a two-choice discrimination task to show how perceived duration could shift from the actual duration.",
