      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that the point of subjective equality is a “comparison value at which a person judges two stimuli as equal,” but the supplied packet only says that PSE was “derived from individual psychometric functions” in a two-alternative forced-choice discrimination task; it does not explicitly describe PSE in those “comparison value/judges two stimuli as equal” terms.",
        "The packet does support that, in this study, PSE was derived from individual psychometric functions in a two-choice task and related to perceived versus objective duration (e.g., between-group intervals perceived as longer than objective duration), but because the first sentence’s core characterization is not directly supported by the packet, the overall definition is not fully defensible."
